title: Story_01_Intro
---
Terminal: NEW ASSIGNMENT RECEIVED. COORDINATES ATTACHED.
Terminal: SALVAGE PRIORITY: LOW. QUOTA DEADLINE: 40 CYCLES.
Terminal: SENTENCE STATUS: SUSPENDED. REVIEW PENDING ON QUOTA.
Jim: "Pending." They love that word.
Jim: Alright. Time to move.
===

title: Story_02_Departure
---
Jim: Course locked. Nothing out here but me and the dark.
Jim: Let's see what the void left me this time.
===

title: Story_03_Arrival
---
Jim: These are the coordinates. Whatever's left of it, it's right here.
Jim: Hooks out. Let's get this over with.
===

title: Story_04_Haul
---
Jim: ...Scrap. Half a ton of scrap and a cracked coolant cell.
Jim: Months. Months since I pulled anything worth the fuel.
Jim: The Corporation doesn't fire people. It just stops suspending the sentence.
Jim: Keep this up and I don't lose the job. I lose my head.
Jim: How did I even end up out here.
===

title: Flashback_Recruitment
---
Guard: On your feet. You've got a visitor.
Officer: Jim. Convicted. Sentenced. Scheduled.
Officer: I'm not here to appeal any of that.
Officer: The Corporation has an opening. Salvage work. Deep field, long hauls, no crew.
Jim: And if I say no?
Officer: Then the schedule stands.
Officer: Say yes, and the sentence is suspended. Not commuted. Suspended.
Officer: You keep it suspended by making quota.
-> Where do I sign?
    Officer: You don't sign anything. You stop being a problem and start being an asset.
-> What happens when I miss quota?
    Officer: Then you're a problem again.
-> How long is the contract?
    Officer: There's no end date. There's only the next quota.
===

title: Story_05_Contact
---
Terminal: PROXIMITY ALERT. VESSEL ON DRIFT COURSE.
Terminal: TRANSPONDER: INDEPENDENT SALVAGE. HAILING CHANNEL OPEN.
Jim: Someone out here actually wants to talk. That's new.
===

title: Scavenger_Encounter
---
<<if reputation("Scavengers") >= 25>>
    <<jump Scavenger_Encounter_Friendly>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Scavenger_Encounter_Hostile>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Scavenger_Encounter_Friendly
---
Vee: Hey! How've you been? Pulled anything worth hauling lately?
Vee: Ever since they raised the quotas, this job has been a grind.
Vee: I upgraded my radar. Now I get more coordinates than I can fly to — you should stop putting that off.
Vee: Here, take one. Two pings came in at once, opposite ends of the sector. Someone's going to beat me to the other one anyway. Better it's you.
-> Thanks. I owe you one.
    Vee: Just don't get yourself blown up out there.
-> Why hand it over?
    Vee: Because I can't be in two places. And I'd rather it went to you than to some Corporation lapdog.
===

title: Scavenger_Encounter_Hostile
---
Vee: Well. If it isn't Jim.
Vee: Struck out again, I take it? Good. Keep it up.
Vee: One of these days something out here just blows you apart, and the Corporation files it as attrition.
Vee: Fewer of us, more scrap for me.
-> ...
    Vee: Yeah. That's what I thought.
===
